  "body": "Is the current Metal 4 already implemented to support the new Tensor APIs for Neural Accelerators?\n\nhttps://developer.apple.com/metal/whats-new/\n\n> ### Metal 4 machine learning\n> \n> Tensors are now a native resource type you can use to operate on data.\n\nhttps://www.macrumors.com/guide/m4-vs-m5-chip/\n\n> - 4×+ peak GPU compute performance for AI\n> - 3.6× faster time to first token (LLM)\n\n[Demystifying Apple’s AMX AI accelerator: when and why it outperforms the GPU](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TjfA9LVgHXk)",
